{"name":"Seaport Steam","hex":"#aecac8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"seaport","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A town or harbour with facilities for seagoing ships to dock and take on or discharge cargo."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seaport"},{"term":"steam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The hot gaseous form of water, formed when water changes from the liquid phase to the gas phase (at or above its boiling point temperature).","The suspended condensate (cloud) formed by water vapour when it encounters colder air.\nMist, fog.\nExhaled breath into cold air below the dew point of the exhalation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook with steam.","To be cooked with steam."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/steam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Port","blocks":[{"text":"A port is a maritime facility comprising one or more wharves or loading areas, where ships load and discharge cargo and passengers. Although usually situated on a sea coast or estuary, ports can also be found far inland, such as Hamburg, Manchester and Duluth; these access the sea via rivers or canals. Because of their roles as ports of entry for immigrants as well as soldiers in wartime, many port cities have experienced dramatic multi-ethnic and multicultural changes throughout their histories."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/View_of_Nam_Harbor_from_Busan_Tower.jpg/330px-View_of_Nam_Harbor_from_Busan_Tower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port"},{"title":"Steam","blocks":[{"text":"Steam is water vapor, often mixed with air and/or an aerosol of liquid water droplets. This may occur by evaporation or by boiling, where heat is applied until water reaches the enthalpy of vaporization. Superheated or saturated steam is invisible; however, wet steam, a visible mist or aerosol of water droplets, is often referred to as \"steam\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg/330px-Steam_phase_eruption_of_Castle_Geyser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Steam"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Manhattan.jpg/500px-Manhattan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Manhattan.jpg/1280px-Manhattan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Manhattan.jpg/500px-Manhattan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Port of New York and New Jersey, U.S., grew from the original harbor at the convergence of the Hudson River and the East River at the Upper New York Bay.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManhattan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/La_Lanterna_di_Genova_di_notte.jpg/500px-La_Lanterna_di_Genova_di_notte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/La_Lanterna_di_Genova_di_notte.jpg/1280px-La_Lanterna_di_Genova_di_notte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/La_Lanterna_di_Genova_di_notte.jpg/500px-La_Lanterna_di_Genova_di_notte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The ancient Port of Genoa, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALa_Lanterna_di_Genova_di_notte.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Frigidarium_Terme_del_Foro_Ostia_Antica_2006-09-08.jpg/500px-Frigidarium_Terme_del_Foro_Ostia_Antica_2006-09-08.jpg?utm_source=en